<title>UK: Castle Transmission sets 125 mln stg 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Castle Transmission sets 125 mln stg 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Credit Suisse First Boston and J.P. Morgan Securities.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CASTLE TRANSMISSION FINANCE PLC</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  CASTLE TRANSMISSION INTERNATIONAL AND</p>
<p>		CASTLE TRANSMISSION HOLDINGS LTD</p>
<p> AMT    125 MLN STG   COUPON     9.00	MATURITY   *30.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.161    PAY DATE    21.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    99.161    SPREAD	+195 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALL OR PUT AT ANY TIME, PUT AT 101.00.</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND =</p>
<p> NOTES	BORROWER IS A CONSORTIUM LED BY CASTLE TOWER</p>
<p>		CORPORATION (CTC) OF THE U.S. WHICH BOUGHT BRITAIN'S</p>
<p>		STATE-OWNED BBC'S DOMESTIC RADIO AND TELEVISION</p>
<p>		TRANSMISSION NETWORK FOR 244 MILLION STG IN FEBRUARY.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
